        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In respect of that, he has placed reliance over the judgment of Board of Control for Cricket in India vs. Netaji Cricket Club and Others reported in (2005) 4 Supreme Court Cases 741 (Para 90 & 93 ) and further the judgment of Division Bench"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f8d4524e9d0a48e4be24d037515b0ad8_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is further submitted that Division Bench relying the judgment of Apex Court in the cases of Moinuddin and BCCI (supra).\n"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bdaf243ba8cb4d80b94737912f120f09_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Considering the aforesaid, we do not find any merit in the aforesaid contention firstly that there is no affidavit of counsel represented the petitioner in the writ petition and that the complete copy of license was handed over to the petit"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "781bcf1f62414eff9f218baa92ed8cca_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Upon perusal of the review petition, we also do not find any averment that complete copy of license was filed along with E- Tender before the respondents."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2872cc594f5a46eeba22edf9bc8e1c8b_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe judgment which has been relied by the NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-IND:28927 3 RP-860-2024 counsel for petitioner would not render any assistance to the facts of the present case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fac37f1b406c4712bd93d17b0b79490d_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the judgment of Moinuddin which has been relied by the Division Bench in the case of Juber has dealt with the case of Habeas Corpus petition and it is held that if there is insufficient pleading, the review can be entertained."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "250c1cefe85849769f7d4c6b24a8c5ef_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The judgment passed in the case of BCCI (supra) in para 90, the Apex Court has considered the word \"sufficient reason\" for reviewing of the order and held that word 'sufficient reason' would depend on the facts of the present case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "546386c512544e148b821f1489189cdf_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThus, we do not find any error apparent on the face of the record warranting any interference in exercise of review power."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "eb389228f7914bff96a056b58b7a1b04_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is well settled that cases are heard and decided only once."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0f6f682d1c654244a19880fe9765ae63_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "To make a departure from this statutory rule, review application must strictly fall within the established parameters."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7f1adc317e264ff3a7b0274ef1a53faa_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the light of settled principle of law in my considered opinion, there is no merit and substance in the review application as in a review, Court has very limited circumscribed by definitive limits."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2d6e0f56b8804ff3bd480341cea4caaa_27",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nAccordingly, the review application is dismissed."
      }
